v1.4.4
- Shared users: a user shared to other nodes is held by all of them alike (any holder edits, shares on, leaves or deletes it everywhere; traffic summed against one limit); "Accept shared users" setting
- Automatic update (off by default): daily at a set time; optionally fetched from a node that already runs the new release
- User details dialog has the list's actions (enable, reset traffic, share, delete)
- Tools: Stop really stops; the throughput line animates each sample; terminal copy / paste / select all keys
- Nodes behind one NAT are no longer taken for a rename; a node whose registration was dropped registers again

v1.4.3
- System traffic capture puts back rules another program removed (e.g. systemd-networkd restarted by an unattended upgrade)
- Punch interface: a node accepting punches chooses the interface they use (Interfaces page); changing it re-punches
- Hole punching on built-in child interfaces
- hy2scale:// node links: all public addresses and punch relays; the import detects hy2scale and hysteria2 links

v1.4.2
- UniFi OS gateways: interfaces follow the gateway's network setup (ports, LANs, WANs with child interfaces); install script platform under /data
- Default gateways from policy-routing tables; host network detected outside containers; server certificate paths fixed for non-Docker installs
- In-app upgrade on systemd installs; release versions are newer than their pre-releases
- Speed test over several exit paths (quality / aggregate)
- Rules: import and export (YAML), experimental graph editor
- Key badge on nodes you can manage; punch can fill the peer's password
- WireGuard peer details have an Edit button

v1.4.1
- Hole punching: failure reasons tell a target's setting from a symmetric NAT, on either side; reflectors may be left empty; Punch button in the topology
- Capture: local subnets are reached directly (Docker containers), works behind a host INPUT DROP firewall (ufw), 1.3.x rules left after an in-place upgrade are removed
- Address and punch status follow the live connections
- Topology: auto layouts stay put while open; click a line to select it; map lines can cross into the next copy of the world
- Trojan certificate chosen from the TLS list; self-built versions marked with '*'

v1.4.0
- VPN servers (L2TP/IPsec, IKEv2, OpenVPN, WireGuard) run in userspace, no privileges needed
- Policy sets and condition sets replace IP/domain rules; transparent capture of local and forwarded traffic
- Trojan server; OpenVPN over TCP, compression framing, pushed routes
- Per-user upload/download rate limits, traffic reset periods
- Hole punching between nodes behind NAT; per-address outgoing interface
- Overview, Interfaces, Tools, Audit and Logs pages; world map view of nodes
- In-app upgrade kept across app restarts on iKuai

v1.3.x
- See https://github.com/FrankoonG/hy2scale/releases

v1.2.2
- Added TUN mode IP packet forwarding (rules advanced mode)
- Fixed TCP proxy splitting connections breaking ENC-RTSP authentication
- Fixed rules UDP proxy conntrack return routing
- Added rules Advanced tab with TUN toggle and mode selector
- Support TUN/redirect hot switching

v1.2.1
- Added rules UDP forwarding support
- Added WireGuard UDP exit routing
- Fixed idle timeout causing stuck requests
- Fixed multi-hop UDP relay

v1.2.0
- Added IP/domain routing rules engine
- Added WireGuard userspace VPN
- IKEv2 compat mode (xfrm bridge)
- L2TP TUN capture mode
